  "question": {
    "text": "Let $a=1+\\frac{{ }^2 \\mathrm{C}_2}{3 !}+\\frac{{ }^3 \\mathrm{C}_2}{4 !}+\\frac{{ }^4 \\mathrm{C}_2}{5 !}+\\ldots$,\n$\\mathrm{b}=1+\\frac{{ }^1 \\mathrm{C}_0+{ }^1 \\mathrm{C}_1}{1 !}+\\frac{{ }^2 \\mathrm{C}_0+{ }^2 \\mathrm{C}_1+{ }^2 \\mathrm{C}_2}{2 !}+\\frac{{ }^3 \\mathrm{C}_0+{ }^3 \\mathrm{C}_1+{ }^3 \\mathrm{C}_2+{ }^3 \\mathrm{C}_3}{3 !}+\\ldots$<br />Then $\\frac{2 b}{a^2}$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "8",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{f}(\\mathrm{x})=1+\\frac{(1+\\mathrm{x})}{1 !}+\\frac{(1+\\mathrm{x})^2}{2 !}+\\frac{(1+\\mathrm{x})^3}{3 !}+\\ldots . . \\\\\n& \\frac{\\mathrm{e}^{(1+\\mathrm{x})}}{1+\\mathrm{x}}=\\frac{1}{1+\\mathrm{x}}+1+\\frac{(1+\\mathrm{x})}{2 !}+\\frac{(1+\\mathrm{x})^2}{3 !}+\\frac{(1+\\mathrm{x})^2}{4 !} \\\\\n& \\text { coef } \\mathrm{x}^2 \\text { in RHS : } 1+\\frac{{ }^2 \\mathrm{C}_2}{3}+\\frac{{ }^3 \\mathrm{C}_2}{4}+\\ldots=\\mathrm{a}\n\\end{aligned}$\ncoeff. $x^2$ in L.H.S.\n$e\\left(1+x+\\frac{x^2}{2 !}\\right) \\ldots\\left(1-x+\\frac{x^2}{2 !} \\ldots \\ldots\\right)$\nis $\\mathrm{e}-\\mathrm{e}+\\frac{\\mathrm{e}}{2 !}=\\mathrm{a}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{b}=1+\\frac{2}{1 !}+\\frac{2^2}{2 !}+\\frac{2^3}{3 !}+\\ldots \\ldots=\\mathrm{e}^2 \\\\\n& \\frac{2 \\mathrm{~b}}{\\mathrm{a}^2}=8\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
